    "# CPI-Surprise Trading Strategy: Quantitative Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** Yogen Mudgal  \n",
    "**Date:** 2024-2025  \n",
    "**Course:** FBE 551 (Advanced Quantitative Finance)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Executive Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook presents a systematic analysis of a macroeconomic-driven trading strategy based on Consumer Price Index (CPI) surprises. The strategy trades SPY (S&P 500) and QQQ (Nasdaq-100) based on whether actual CPI inflation comes in above or below market expectations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Findings:**\n",
    "- Negative CPI surprises signal buying opportunities in equity markets on an intraday and next-day basis\n",
    "- Without transaction costs, the strategy generates positive Sharpe ratios (0.24-0.38)\n",
    "- Transaction costs significantly erode returns, reducing edge to near-zero\n",
    "- Post-COVID period (2020-2024) shows improved performance (0.66 Sharpe for SPY intraday)\n",
    "- Factor regression analysis finds statistically insignificant alpha after controlling for standard risk factors\n"
   ]
  },
